### What the flow does

```
[Receive Invoice] → [Extract Invoice Fields (InvoiceIXP)] → [Build Invoice Record] → [Invoice Processed ✓]
                                        ↓ (on error)
                               [Extraction Failed ✗]
```

| Node | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Receive Invoice** | Manual trigger — accepts an `invoiceFile` reference as input to kick off processing |
| **Extract Invoice Fields** | Runs your invoice document through the **InvoiceIXP** AI extraction model (already published on your tenant in the `Shared` folder). Automatically reads vendor name, invoice number, dates, totals, line items, and more. |
| **Build Invoice Record** | Script node that collects the extracted fields into a clean, structured object with normalized field names (`invoiceNumber`, `vendorName`, `totalAmount`, `lineItems`, etc.) |
| **Invoice Processed** | Happy-path end — outputs the structured `invoiceRecord` |
| **Extraction Failed** | Error-path end — fires if the IxP model fails (bad file, service error, etc.) |

### The output `invoiceRecord` contains:
`invoiceNumber` · `invoiceDate` · `dueDate` · `vendorName` · `vendorAddress` · `billToName` · `subtotal` · `taxAmount` · `totalAmount` · `currency` · `purchaseOrderNumber` · `lineItems[]` · `documentId` · `extractedAt`

---

